// Verus solution for the permutation check problem.
//
// We only consider s[0], s[1], s[2]. Input is length 3 or 4, and if 4 then s[3] == '\n'.
// Each of the first three chars is in {'a','b','c'}.
// Return "Yes\n" iff the first three are pairwise distinct; else "No\n".

#![allow(unused_imports)]
